-- A static `ToolDefinition` has its `inputSchema` compiled once at `register` time, so a schema that is not valid JSON Schema throws synchronously from `register` with an error message naming the offending tool ([validated by names the tool when a static schema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L206), [validated by throws at register time naming the tool when a static inputSchema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L94)).
-- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled at `register` time and reused on every `execute` call without re-reading or re-compiling `definition.inputSchema` ([validated by compiles a static schema once at registration and reuses it across executions](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L258)).
-- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves its definition on each `execute` call and validates against the `inputSchema` returned for that call, caching compiled validators by schema object reference (`WeakMap`) so distinct returned schemas each enforce their own rules. ([validated by caches a function-valued schema validator by object reference](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L225))
